// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`the bridge keeps its id with the new door (S50b) > cloudEraseHeld is an optional door with no arguments 1`] = `"S50b (US-25 AC16i): a Promise of one word, asked before Disconnect or a switch closes anything. It flushes the open session first, as a close does, then says whether an erase made on this phone is still unsent: 'none' (no session, no such erase, or a save has carried it), 'transient' (its last save failed with no answer, 408, 429, a 5xx, Drive's rate or daily limit, or a 401 whose token refresh was skipped), 'definite' (any other failure: storage full, a refused sign-in, another 4xx) or 'unknown' (it failed and no report said why). Only 'transient' holds the Disconnect; the app runs today's path on every other word and on one it does not know. cloudClose's answers are unchanged. An engine before it has no such door: optionalCall answers nil and Disconnect runs as before, never a crash."`;
